      "description": "Watch Brann vs PAOK highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The UEFA Conference League delivered a night of high-octane football on August 27, 2026, as Brann and PAOK locked horns in a clash defined by momentum shifts and tactical battles. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish dominance, setting the stage for a match that would keep fans on the edge of their seats until the very last second. Late First-Half Breakthrough The opening period was a physical affair, with both teams struggling to find a clear path through well-organized defenses. The tension was evident early on when Tom Louchet received a yellow card in the 37th minute. However, the deadlock was finally broken in stoppage time of the first half. In the 45+3 minute, Niklas Castro turned provider, delivering a sharp ball to Noah Holm , who clinical finish gave Brann a crucial lead heading into the interval. A Whirlwind Second Half The momentum stayed with the hosts as the second half got underway, and they doubled their advantage in the 57th minute. Kristian Eriksen set up Kristall Mani Ingason , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. Yet, the 2-0 lead proved fragile as PAOK launched a spirited comeback. Cherif Ndiaye pulled one back in the 63rd minute following an assist from Dimitrios Pelkas , and just four minutes later, Christos Zafeiris leveled the score at 2-2, capitalising on a pass from Dimitrios Chatsidis . Castro Clinches the Win With the match hanging in the balance and the atmosphere reaching a fever pitch, the final ten minutes were filled with tactical changes and disciplinary interventions. The decisive moment arrived in the 86th minute when Brann were awarded a penalty. Niklas Castro , having already assisted the opener, stepped up and calmly converted from the spot to restore the lead. Despite a frantic period of added time that saw yellow cards for Ulrik Mathisen and Dimitrios Pelkas , Brann held firm to secure a memorable 3-2 victory."
